From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 04:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gcs: ship the licences of the statically linked dependencies

libstreamergcs.so statically links google-cloud-cpp and everything it
pulls in through bazel (abseil, protobuf, gRPC, BoringSSL, libcurl,
zlib, c-ares, re2, crc32c, nlohmann/json, ...), but the explicit
license_files=("LICENSE",) only ships the project's own licence. The
BSD/MIT/curl/OpenSSL licences and the Apache-2.0 NOTICE files require
their notices to travel with the binary. Also match LICENSE.* next to
setup.py, where the build stages each dependency's licence text.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [this port does not open issues/PRs against third-party repos; the upstream wheels have the same gap]
---
 py/runai_model_streamer_gcs/setup.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/py/runai_model_streamer_gcs/setup.py b/py/runai_model_streamer_gcs/setup.py
index 1379a4f..03f2ff3 100644
--- a/py/runai_model_streamer_gcs/setup.py
+++ b/py/runai_model_streamer_gcs/setup.py
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@ assert_lib_exists()
 setup(
     name="runai-model-streamer-gcs",
     version=VERSION,
-    license_files=("LICENSE",),
+    license_files=("LICENSE", "LICENSE.*"),
     packages=find_packages(),
     install_requires=["google-cloud-storage", "google-auth"],
     data_files=[("/runai_model_streamer/libstreamer/lib/", [LIB])],
-- 
